        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "# Demo 2b: Where Trees Cool Most – Geographically Weighted Regression (GWR) with Spatial AI (OML4Py)",
          "",
          "**HrOUG 2026 · Spatial Meets AI** · Which ZET stops need shade first?",
          "",
          "The LISA notebook showed where Zagreb is hot. This notebook asks what drives the heat, and whether the answer is the same everywhere: **spatial heterogeneity**. One global regression gives one effect of tree canopy for the whole city. A geographically weighted regression (GWR) fits a local regression around every H3 cell, so the effect of trees can differ from one part of the city to another.",
          "",
          "It answers three questions:",
          "1. **How much do trees cool on average?** A global OLS regression of surface temperature on land cover, with spatial diagnostics.",
          "2. **Do trees cool the same everywhere?** GWR: the local cooling effect of tree canopy for every H3 cell, on a map.",
          "3. **What if?** 15 percentage points of tree canopy instead of built-up area at a stop: how much cooler does its cell get, at stops in different parts of the city?",
          "",
          "Adapted from the Oracle sample notebook *OML4Py Spatial AI GWR Regressor* (Copyright (c) 2025 Oracle Corporation, [The Universal Permissive License (UPL), Version 1.0](https://oss.oracle.com/licenses/upl/))."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
