          "%md",
          "",
          "###### 1. How much do trees cool on average?",
          "",
          "A global OLS regression explains the surface temperature of each cell with its share of tree canopy and other green. Built-up area is the reference category, so each coefficient means \"one percentage point of this land cover instead of built-up area\", in °C. The intercept is the temperature of a fully built-up cell. Water (0.8 % of the city) counts with built-up area; see the note in section 2.",
          "",
          "With spatial weights (the 6 nearest cells), the summary adds spatial diagnostics. A significant Moran's I of the residuals means the global model leaves a spatial pattern unexplained. That is the bridge to GWR."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
