          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<h6 id=\"1-how-much-do-trees-cool-on-average\">1. How much do trees cool on average?</h6>\n<p>A global OLS regression explains the surface temperature of each cell with its share of tree canopy and other green. Built-up area is the reference category, so each coefficient means &quot;one percentage point of this land cover instead of built-up area&quot;, in °C. The intercept is the temperature of a fully built-up cell. Water (0.8 % of the city) counts with built-up area; see the note in section 2.</p>\n<p>With spatial weights (the 6 nearest cells), the summary adds spatial diagnostics. A significant Moran's I of the residuals means the global model leaves a spatial pattern unexplained. That is the bridge to GWR.</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
        "relations" : [ ],
