          "%md",
          "",
          "###### 2. Do trees cool the same everywhere?",
          "",
          "GWR fits a local regression for every H3 cell from its neighbourhood. The neighbourhood is adaptive: the 200 nearest cells, about 21 km² or a radius of 2.5 km. Every cell gets its own coefficients (`betas`).",
          "",
          "Training fits about 6,000 local models and takes longer than OLS. Without a spatial weights definition, GWR searches for the optimal bandwidth, which takes much longer still."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
