            {
              "message" : "<h6 id=\"2-do-trees-cool-the-same-everywhere\">2. Do trees cool the same everywhere?</h6>\n<p>GWR fits a local regression for every H3 cell from its neighbourhood. The neighbourhood is adaptive: the 200 nearest cells, about 21 km² or a radius of 2.5 km. Every cell gets its own coefficients (<code>betas</code>).</p>\n<p>Training fits about 6,000 local models and takes longer than OLS. Without a spatial weights definition, GWR searches for the optimal bandwidth, which takes much longer still.</p>\n",
