        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "The local coefficient of `CANOPY_PCT` says how much cooler a cell gets with more trees instead of built-up area, in that part of the city. The map shows it as °C cooler per +10 percentage points of canopy: the darker, the more a tree buys.",
          "",
          "Why water is not a model variable: in about half of the neighbourhoods of 200 cells there is no water at all. A variable that is 0 in every neighbour cannot be estimated, and the local regression fails with a singular matrix. Water therefore counts with built-up area.",
          "",
          "Where a land cover hardly varies within a neighbourhood, its local coefficient is uncertain. In the forest of Medvednica, canopy and other green add up to almost 100 % in every cell, so read the canopy map as a whole, not single extreme cells."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
