        "result" : {
          "interpreter" : "md.low",
          "taskStatus" : "SUCCESS",
          "status" : "SUCCESS",
          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<p>The local coefficient of <code>CANOPY_PCT</code> says how much cooler a cell gets with more trees instead of built-up area, in that part of the city. The map shows it as °C cooler per +10 percentage points of canopy: the darker, the more a tree buys.</p>\n<p>Why water is not a model variable: in about half of the neighbourhoods of 200 cells there is no water at all. A variable that is 0 in every neighbour cannot be estimated, and the local regression fails with a singular matrix. Water therefore counts with built-up area.</p>\n<p>Where a land cover hardly varies within a neighbourhood, its local coefficient is uncertain. In the forest of Medvednica, canopy and other green add up to almost 100 % in every cell, so read the canopy map as a whole, not single extreme cells.</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
        "relations" : [ ],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
